&lt;p&gt;At Axon, we’re on a mission to Protect Life. We’re explorers, pursuing society’s most critical safety and justice issues with our ecosystem of devices and cloud software. Like our products, we work better together. We connect with candor and care, seeking out diverse perspectives from our customers, communities and each other.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Life at Axon is fast-paced, challenging and meaningful. Here, you’ll take ownership and drive real change. Constantly grow as you work hard for a mission that matters at a company where you matter.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Impact &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Order Management Analyst, you will play a critical role in ensuring the accuracy, efficiency, and integrity of Axon’s order-to-cash operations. You will independently manage a complex process of bookings workflows while partnering cross-functionally with Sales, Finance, Fulfillment, Product, and Customer Success teams to deliver an exceptional customer experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: &lt;/strong&gt;Onsite at one of our Axon Hubs Tuesday-Friday.&amp;nbsp; (Axon Hubs: San Francisco (Presidio), Seattle, Scottsdale, NYC, Atlanta, Sterling, Boston).&amp;nbsp; The ideal candidate will be able to work in a West Coast hub and cover west coast hours.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to: &lt;/strong&gt;Director, Order Management&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently manage end-to-end order processing including order validation, booking, amendments, system corrections, and releases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and interpret contracts, pricing structures, and commercial terms to ensure accurate order entry and revenue integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve complex order issues impacting bookings, fulfillment, invoicing, or compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales, Sales Operations, Finance (AR), Fulfillment Team, and Product teams to remove blockers and drive timely fulfillment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform internal audits and quality checks to ensure compliance with revenue controls and operational standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement initiatives, including automation and workflow optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver process training and mentor junior analysts to elevate team capability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to pipeline reviews and provide operational insight that supports revenue forecasting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in Order Management, Revenue Operations, or Order-to-Cash environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to independently manage complex global transactions with minimal supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of revenue controls, audit requirements, and booking compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in ERP and CRM systems (e.g., Salesforce, D365, SAP, NetSuite, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills and experience using reporting tools (Excel, Sigma, or similar platforms).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence cross-functional stakeholders and drive resolution in ambiguous situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous improvement mindset with experience implementing process enhancements or automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
