&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join Axon and be a Force for Good.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Axon, we’re on a mission to Protect Life. We’re explorers, pursuing society’s most critical safety and justice issues with our ecosystem of devices and cloud software. Like our products, we work better together. We connect with candor and care, seeking out diverse perspectives from our customers, communities and each other.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Life at Axon is fast-paced, challenging and meaningful. Here, you’ll take ownership and drive real change. Constantly grow as you work hard for a mission that matters at a company where you matter.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Description - Principal Security Operations Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our mission is to protect life&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re out to make the world a safer place by solving big problems and taking on the public safety challenges of our time. From our company&#39;s inception building the TASER device to a full suite of hardware and software solutions, we are focused on providing police agencies with state-of-the-art devices and services they need to successfully serve and protect us. In the next few years, we&#39;re going to eliminate the burden of paperwork in policing, so officers can increase the time they spend building relationships and serving in their communities. We’ll put video at the heart of police records so our justice system can get to the truth faster. And we won&#39;t stop innovating until the bullet is rendered obsolete. It’s a big mission, but it’s one we’ll pursue relentlessly every single day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Principal&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Security Operations Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;, you will play a key role in building secure, reliable, and developer-friendly infrastructure that enables teams to move quickly without compromising security. You will solve complex technical challenges, improve system reliability through automation, and partner closely with engineering teams to scale security capabilities across the organization. In this role, you will design and develop security tools that support vulnerability management and secure software delivery pipelines, integrating security seamlessly into developer workflows. Your work will help reduce friction for developers while ensuring high standards for security, reliability, and operational efficiency across mission-critical systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Seattle, WA, Scottsdale, AZ, Boston, MA, Atlanta, GA, San Francisco, CA&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct Reports:&lt;/strong&gt; None&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Day-to-Day&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the review, design, and continuous improvement of Axon’s Kubernetes platforms with platform teams to strengthen architecture, security, resilience, and operational practices across existing and new environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the evolution of security application delivery at Axon, refactoring how security services are built, deployed, and operated while establishing automated security controls and guardrails across CI/CD pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect, provision, and secure AWS and Azure infrastructure supporting critical security platforms and services, leveraging infrastructure-as-code, automation, and cloud-native best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with developers, SRE, and platform engineering teams to influence architecture and ensure security is embedded into infrastructure, services, and developer workflows by design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide deep technical leadership during complex security and infrastructure incidents, driving root cause analysis, durable remediation, and engineering improvements that prevent recurrence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advance security observability across cloud and Kubernetes environments through improved telemetry, logging, metrics, detection, and actionable alerting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to eliminate operational toil by building and improving internal security tooling, automation, runbooks, and self-service capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish technical standards and best practices for operating security platforms at scale, while mentoring engineers and influencing technical direction across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or operating PKI and certificate management systems at scale is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and drive the technical strategy for securing Axon’s cloud-native infrastructure, with a strong focus on Kubernetes, containerized workloads, and AWS/Azure environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead architectural reviews and improvements across Axon’s Kubernetes platforms, identifying security, reliability, and operational gaps and partnering with platform teams to implement scalable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modernize how security applications are built, deployed, and operated at Axon, improving deployment architecture, automation, CI/CD pipelines, and infrastructure-as-code to create secure, repeatable, and resilient delivery patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement security guardrails and automated controls across CI/CD and developer workflows, enabling engineering teams to move quickly while identifying and addressing security risks early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and provision secure, highly available AWS and Azure infrastructure for critical security services using infrastructure-as-code and cloud-native technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and improve security standards for Kubernetes and container ecosystems, including cluster hardening, workload security, RBAC, network controls, admission policies, image security, and runtime protection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical leadership for complex security and infrastructure challenges, including high-impact incidents, architecture decisions, and cross-platform security initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with SRE, Platform Engineering, Product Security, and development teams to influence technical direction and embed security into platform architecture and engineering practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive improvements in security observability, automation, and operational resilience while reducing manual processes and engineering toil.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers, establish engineering best practices, and raise the technical bar for building and operating security platforms across Axon.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply PKI and certificate management expertise where applicable to strengthen security architecture and platform capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;what you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in security engineering, platform engineering, infrastructure, SRE, or related roles, with demonstrated technical leadership across large-scale environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level Kubernetes experience, with deep hands-on knowledge of cluster architecture, provisioning, upgrades, networking, RBAC, policy enforcement, workload security, and operating production Kubernetes environments at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience reviewing and improving existing Kubernetes platforms, identifying architectural and security gaps, and driving improvements across multiple engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in AWS and/or Azure, including designing, provisioning, securing, and operating highly available cloud infrastructure using infrastructure-as-code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong software engineering and automation skills, with proficiency in languages such as Go, Python, or similar, and experience building production-grade internal platforms, services, and security tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience designing and improving CI/CD and application deployment architectures, including refactoring legacy deployment patterns into secure, automated, repeatable, and scalable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of container security and container registries such as ECR and ACR, including image lifecycle, vulnerability scanning, access controls, and supply chain security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of cloud-native security architecture, including network security, secrets management, workload identity, policy enforcement, and runtime protection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing security guardrails and automated controls that improve security while minimizing friction for developers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong infrastructure-as-code experience with technologies such as Terraform, Helm, GitOps, or similar tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to troubleshoot complex distributed systems and lead technical response to high-impact security, infrastructure, and production incidents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing security observability capabilities across cloud and Kubernetes environments, including logging, metrics, detection, and actionable alerting.&lt;/li&gt;
