&lt;li&gt;Substantial hands-on hardware bring-up and debugging experience using wireless communications testers, spectrum analyzers, oscilloscopes, network analyzers, signal generators, power supplies, and related RF/electrical test equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with antenna, mechanical, firmware, and systems engineers to optimize end-to-end wireless performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience taking wireless hardware from concept and architecture through validation, certification, manufacturing ramp, and mass production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with applicable U.S. and international wireless, EMC, regulatory, carrier, or safety certification requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience working directly with silicon and chipset vendors, ODMs, JDMs, CMs, and external engineering partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexibility to travel domestically up to 50% of the time, as needed, to support the team.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
