&lt;li&gt;Coach individual contributors through complex technical decisions, ambiguous customer problems, executive conversations, and high-stakes delivery moments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear expectations for ownership, technical quality, onsite partnership, production delivery, adoption, documentation, and measurable agency impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build individualized development plans and create opportunities for Mission Engineers to expand their technical range, executive presence, and transformation leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of curiosity, candor, responsible experimentation, continuous learning, and shared accountability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support thoughtful team growth by selecting and onboarding people who can both build practical solutions and earn credibility with agency stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Set the Bar for Agency Outcomes&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure Mission Engineers begin with the agency’s mission, operational workflow, and desired outcome before selecting or building a solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Require clear baselines, success criteria, and adoption measures so impact is demonstrated rather than assumed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide the team from discovery through production use, iteration, handoff, and sustained adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help Mission Engineers balance immediate agency needs with secure, maintainable, and scalable solution design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reinforce that success means the agency is more capable—not that one individual has become indispensable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Own a Strategic Mission Engineering Portfolio&lt;/h3&gt;
